! C22-6578 PROBLEM 3.1, "SEPARATION INTO INTEGER AND FRACTION PARTS",
! printed p.26 (PDF 27), read in the ink.
!
!   "The floating-point number N in location DOG has a small (<=48)
!   exponent magnitude.  Create two normalized floating-point numbers
!   I, F in CAT, CAT+1 respectively such that: I = an integer;
!   |F| < 1.0, sign of F = sign of N; and I + F = N."
!
!   Method 1.   DL(U), DOG
!               D+(U), X48
!               ST(N), CAT
!               SLO(N), CAT + 1.0
!               BEW, $
!       X48     DD(N), 0.0X48           'binary exponent of 48
!
! The six printed statements are the deck's LAST six, as printed.  The
! page prints no DOG and no CAT; those are the deck's.  Blocks A, B and
! C are the same four instructions on other data, with DOG and CAT
! renamed and the BEW left off; nothing else about them is changed.
!
! ASSEMBLED WITH ASM=strap2 (the host STRAP II).  strap_asm.py refuses
! the page's own constant, "DD(N), 0.0X48": see
! decks/problem_3_dd_zero_fraction.strap and docs/NEXT.md.
!
! THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE HAND-DERIVED, from the problem statement and
! the Reference Manual, not from the model:
!   D+(U), X48   printed p.95 (Add Double), by p.86-87's rule: "The
!                fraction of the number with the algebraically smaller
!                exponent is shifted right by the amount of the exponent
!                difference."  X48 has a zero fraction and exponent 48,
!                so N's fraction moves right 48 - e places in the 96-bit
!                fraction: the integer part ends in accumulator bits
!                12-59 and the fraction part begins at bit 60.
!   ST(N), CAT   printed p.90: "the 48-bit operand fraction in the
!                accumulator is normalized before being placed in
!                storage ... Normalization is suppressed when the 48
!                fraction bits are zero."
!   SLO(N)       printed p.97: the fraction is bits 60-107, the exponent
!                is the accumulator's less 48 (here 0), the sign is the
!                accumulator's.
!
!   block   N            I (CAT)                  F (CAT+1)
!   A       -1234.75     -1234 = -.1001101001 x 2^11   -.75 = -.11 x 2^0
!                        0169A40000000008              000C000000000008
!   B       .25          a zero fraction, exponent 48  .25 = .1 x 2^-1
!                        0600000000000000              0038000000000000
!   C       1048581.5    1048581 = (2^20 + 5) x 2^-21 x 2^21
!                        02A8000280000000         .5   0008000000000000
!   last    2.5          2 = .1 x 2^2                  .5 = .1 x 2^0
!                        0048000000000000              0008000000000000
!
! The last is the page's own suggestion, comment (b): "the reader should
! illustrate the program for himself using, for example, N = 2.5".
!
! BLOCK B IS WORTH READING.  For |N| < 1 the page's I is not "normalized":
! the integer part is a zero fraction, ST(N) cannot normalize it, and CAT
! receives an order-of-magnitude zero with exponent 48.  I + F = N still
! holds.  The page's statement asks for "two normalized floating-point
! numbers"; the program delivers one.
!
! tests/problem_3_expected.py works the same four cases from the same
! rules and agrees with the table above.
!
! acc_left_after: word 8 (accumulator bits 0-63) after the last block.
! D+(U) leaves exponent 48 and 2.5 x 2^-48 as a 96-bit fraction: bits
! 12-59 hold 2 and bit 60 holds the half, so the word is
! 0600000000000028.
!
! INJECTION, OBSERVED 2026-11-15 (data side, on a copy of the deck, the
! deck itself untouched): DOGA changed from -4939/4 to -4935/4 (-1233.75).  FAIL A_I only
! (got 0169a20000000008); the other seven CAT checks and the PC
! passed (acc_left_after was not in that run).

START   DL(U), DOGA
        D+(U), X48
        ST(N), CATA
        SLO(N), CATA + 1.0
        DL(U), DOGB
        D+(U), X48
        ST(N), CATB
        SLO(N), CATB + 1.0
        DL(U), DOGC
        D+(U), X48
        ST(N), CATC
        SLO(N), CATC + 1.0
! --- the page, as printed -------------------------------------------
        DL(U), DOG
        D+(U), X48
        ST(N), CAT
        SLO(N), CAT + 1.0
        BEW, $
X48     DD(N), 0.0X48
! --- the deck's data ------------------------------------------------
DOG     DD(N), 5/2
CAT     DR(N), (2)
DOGA    DD(N), -4939/4
CATA    DR(N), (2)
DOGB    DD(N), 1/4
CATB    DR(N), (2)
DOGC    DD(N), 2097163/2
CATC    DR(N), (2)
        END, START
